List the exact supported release branches/versions and their security-update status here. Do not imply support for versions that are not maintained.

| Version | Supported |
|---|---|
| [VERSION] | [YES / NO / END-OF-LIFE DATE] |

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please do not report security vulnerabilities through public issues, discussions, or social media.

Report privately using **[PRIVATE VULNERABILITY REPORTING URL OR SECURITY CONTACT]**. Include affected version/commit, impact, reproduction details, and safe proof-of-concept information. Do not include real user data or live credentials.

## Response expectations

Publish the team's actual acknowledgement, triage, remediation, and disclosure targets here: **[RESPONSE POLICY]**. Do not promise a response window the team cannot meet.

## Disclosure and coordination

Describe the project's coordinated disclosure process, credit policy, release process, and any applicable legal/safety constraints here.

## Scope and safe harbor

Describe authorized assets and prohibited testing. Do not invite denial-of-service, social engineering, physical attacks, privacy violations, or testing against third-party systems.
